:blip r:embed="rId4"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8658535" y="6917216"/><a:ext cx="7764789" cy="4976827"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="51" name="TextBox 50"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{674D6BFD-E2C5-4078-8644-1DF6BDAAB5EE}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8659268" y="12298235"/><a:ext cx="7744968" cy="584775"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx1"/></a:solidFill></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle><a:defPPr><a:defRPr lang="en-US"/></a:defPPr><a:lvl1pPr algn="ctr"><a:defRPr sz="3600" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="FFFF00"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/><a:cs typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/></a:defRPr></a:lvl1pPr></a:lstStyle><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="3200" dirty="0"/><a:t>IoT Architecture </a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="24" name="Picture 23"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{6F781F4A-E307-4A7A-A375-3F9920549802}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId5"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8572108" y="13176097"/><a:ext cx="7773708" cy="6195876"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="53" name="TextBox 52"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{13F8BFFB-E162-449C-9EF5-644C631C27F4}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8614514" y="19589407"/><a:ext cx="7747000" cy="8956298"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="just"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The uploaded image provides a visual representation of the </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" b="1" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>Perception Layer</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>, also known as the Sensor Layer, in IoT systems. This layer collects data from various sensors, including GPS for vehicle tracking, RFID for identifying and monitoring objects, and WSN for infrastructure-free monitoring. The primary function is to gather, detect, and process information before transmitting it to the network layer. Additionally, cameras such as the ESP32-CAM can be used for monitoring and facial recognition, enhancing data collection processes.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="just"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" b="1" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The Network Layer </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>in IoT includes Wi-Fi and Bluetooth for data routing and transmission, with gateways acting as intermediaries to ensure secure, efficient data transfer. Gateways support protocol translation, traffic monitoring, and enhance security alongside firewalls. Additionally, Arduino and ESP32 microcontrollers enable connectivity, while robust servers handle data management and resource sharing across networks.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr algn="just"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" b="1" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>The Application Layer </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>ensures security, data integrity, and confidentiality, facilitating device collaboration and process optimization. It employs communication protocols like SNMP, SOAP, MQTT, </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0" err="1"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>CoAP</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>, AMQP, XMPP, </a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0" err="1"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>mDNS</a:t></a:r><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>, UPnP, and SSDP to enable efficient and secure interaction and service discovery within IoT networks.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="54" name="Picture 53"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{D67C51A7-7C2E-4DE8-9F69-E0BBEDFACDA8}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId2" cstate="print"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{28A0092B-C50C-407E-A947-70E740481C1C}"><a14:useLocalDpi xmlns:a14="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2010/main" val="0"/></a:ext></a:extLst></a:blip><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="148104" y="-630381"/><a:ext cx="4941202" cy="3505040"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="55" name="TextBox 54"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{E5752949-269F-4A46-BBE3-20C76C7AC40D}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8668445" y="28545705"/><a:ext cx="7744968" cy="646331"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx1"/></a:solidFill></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle><a:defPPr><a:defRPr lang="en-US"/></a:defPPr><a:lvl1pPr algn="ctr"><a:defRPr sz="3600" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="FFFF00"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/><a:cs typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/></a:defRPr></a:lvl1pPr></a:lstStyle><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Methodology</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="25" name="Picture 24"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{F4DD8CCF-81B9-4BA6-B4E2-109EB9FD61F6}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId6"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="8678356" y="29353494"/><a:ext cx="7744968" cy="4976827"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="58" name="TextBox 57"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{47202916-6186-4EE0-8AF1-316AF35DF2B9}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="16946401" y="4772337"/><a:ext cx="7747000" cy="5632311"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="just"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>This paper proposes a solution for real-time location capture and transmission using sensors and transition protocols, divided into Machine Learning and IoT sections. The IoT part includes four layers: Sensing, Gateway, Server, and Application. The Sensing layer captures students' faces and geographical locations using high-resolution cameras and GPS devices, ensuring real-time tracking accuracy. The Gateway layer facilitates communication using protocols like HTTPS and MQTT, with ESP32 being preferred for its built-in Wi-Fi and Bluetooth. The Server layer manages data and security, with a preference for cloud servers due to time constraints. The Application layer provides a user-friendly interface for parents, drivers, and school administrators to monitor and manage transportation details, ensuring effective communication and safety.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic><p:nvPicPr><p:cNvPr id="26" name="Picture 25"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{350B86A2-3224-4BB9-97F1-D97ED90AFF1A}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvPicPr><a:picLocks noChangeAspect="1"/></p:cNvPicPr><p:nvPr/></p:nvPicPr><p:blipFill><a:blip r:embed="rId7"/><a:stretch><a:fillRect/></a:stretch></p:blipFill><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="17017309" y="10532593"/><a:ext cx="7676092" cy="4441105"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom></p:spPr></p:pic><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="60" name="TextBox 59"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{124A256B-4B69-4848-A51B-AB61C22D9F42}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="17017309" y="15174092"/><a:ext cx="7747000" cy="4524315"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:noFill/></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:pPr algn="just"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2400" dirty="0"><a:latin typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/><a:cs typeface="Times New Roman" panose="02020603050405020304" pitchFamily="18" charset="0"/></a:rPr><a:t>This figure illustrates the workflow of constructing our model, which includes Data Preparation, Data Pre-processing, and Modeling phases. In Data Preparation, we collect images of targeted children, clean the data by filtering out irrelevant images, normalize histograms, deduplicate data, and validate the dataset. During Data Pre-processing, we select specific facial features for the model to focus on, ensuring the dataset is well-structured for machine learning. The Modeling phase involves training the model using CNN, testing its efficacy with specified images, and simulating student journeys to measure performance. Any discovered errors are then finalized and corrected.</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="63" name="TextBox 62"><a:extLst><a:ext uri="{FF2B5EF4-FFF2-40B4-BE49-F238E27FC236}"><a16:creationId xmlns:a16="http://schemas.microsoft.com/office/drawing/2014/main" id="{2CC6B8A2-2BAD-40AB-BCC3-BDEEA0C8EC0A}"/></a:ext></a:extLst></p:cNvPr><p:cNvSpPr txBox="1"/><p:nvPr/></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="16991867" y="19698407"/><a:ext cx="7744968" cy="646331"/></a:xfrm><a:prstGeom prst="rect"><a:avLst/></a:prstGeom><a:solidFill><a:schemeClr val="tx1"/></a:solidFill></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr wrap="square" rtlCol="0"><a:spAutoFit/></a:bodyPr><a:lstStyle><a:defPPr><a:defRPr lang="en-US"/></a:defPPr><a:lvl1pPr algn="ctr"><a:defRPr sz="3600" b="1"><a:solidFill><a:srgbClr val="FFFF00"/></a:solidFill><a:latin typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/><a:cs typeface="Aharoni" panose="02010803020104030203" pitchFamily="2" charset="-79"/></a:defRPr></a:lvl1pPr></a:lstStyle><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/><a:t>Design</a:t></a:r></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:pic>